<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Stucco repair in Southeast Calgary covers a lot of newer housing. The City labels Auburn Bay, Mahogany, Rangeview and Seton as 2000s communities and McKenzie Towne as 2010s, and 2021 figures put 17,505 people in McKenzie Towne, with 62% of dwellings built 2001-2010 and 20% built 1991-2000. Older pockets such as Douglasdale/Glen, McKenzie Lake and Riverbend date from the 1980s and 1990s.</p><p>Sandstone Stucco Co is an advertising and introduction service, paid by contractors. It does no stucco work itself; the independent contractor who quotes your job contracts directly with you. If you have hail dents, a woodpecker hole, a crack at a window or crumbling foundation parging, <a href="/stucco-repair-calgary/">start with the stucco repair overview</a> or call (403) 555-0148 for a no-obligation quote.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Do in Southeast Calgary</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">Services for Southeast Calgary Properties</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Stucco Repair & Crack Patching</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Hairline cracks, chips, loose patches and gaps where stucco meets a window or door frame on Southeast Calgary stucco walls. The contractor also has to deal with colour matching on a finish that has weathered.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Hail & Woodpecker Damage</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Hail dents and holes, and northern flicker holes on the wall. A contractor can give you a written repair estimate that you may pass to your insurer, and you call your insurer first.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Foundation Parging</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Cracked or flaking parging on the exposed foundation wall above grade, from a patch to a full-perimeter recoat. Parging only: no foundation crack repair, waterproofing or structural work.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E3D8C6;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(122,90,50,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Oswald',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:700;color:#2A2521;margin:0 0 8px;">Section Replacement & Re-Stucco</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">When damage is widespread or moisture has got behind the finish, a contractor may price a section, an elevation or a full re-stucco. The scope and price come after the wall has been looked at.</p>
      </div>
</div>
<style>
